cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "AeonScript: An open standard for DNA-based information archival"
message: "If you use AeonScript in academic or technical work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Moustapha"
    family-names: "Dramé"
    affiliation: "Independent"
    email: "contact@aeonscript.org"
  - name: "The AeonScript Contributors"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aeonscript-spec/aeonscript"
url: "https://aeonscript.org"
abstract: >-
  AeonScript is a layered, self-describing open standard for archiving
  arbitrary information on synthetic DNA. It defines a 7-layer architecture
  (physical alphabet, multiplexing, random access, error correction, session
  tags, presentation, application), normatively specifies L1, L4, and L5 in
  v0.1, and ships with a Python reference implementation. The project is
  designed to be readable for millennia, owned by no single vendor, and
  governed by archival institutions in the long term.
keywords:
  - "DNA storage"
  - "archival"
  - "open standard"
  - "bioinformatics"
  - "information theory"
  - "Reed-Solomon"
license: "MIT"
license-url: "https://github.com/aeonscript-spec/aeonscript/blob/main/LICENSE"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-06-07"
